  "call": {
    "headline": "Spread out behind Haaland — and bet on the Palmer bounce-back",
    "reasoning": "Haaland (239 points, all of City's penalties, BOU-cry-COV to start) is the anchor and the GW1 captain. The £12.0m Bruno Fernandes stays unbought: Mbeumo, Shaw and Lammens already carry Man Utd's league-best opening run at £17.5m combined, and the money funds a four-strong midfield instead. The conviction bet is Palmer at 10.5% ownership — confirmed on penalties, a 214-point ceiling two seasons back, and a Xabi Alonso reset, with Fulham and Brighton before the Arsenal test. Kerkez and Hume are the cheap structural bets: nailed full-backs on the two best fixture runs outside Manchester. Arsenal assets are deliberately avoided — Saliba and Timber are out and the backline is being rebuilt in the transfer market.",
    "captain": "Haaland",
    "vice": "Palmer",
    "chip": "no chip — Bench Boost and Triple Captain wait for data",
